---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { story, testimonials } from '../data/site.js';

// Prose is plain text between <p> tags — edit it like a document.
// The quotes come from src/data/site.js.
---

<BaseLayout title="Our Story" description="How Helping Hands began and why it still runs.">
  <img class="banner" src={story.bannerImage} alt={story.bannerAlt} />

  <div class="split">
    <div class="split-text">
      <h1>Our Story</h1>

      <p>
        Kushal and Anurag&rsquo;s inspiration to start Helping Hands came in the
        summer of 2020, when the coronavirus pandemic changed the lives of
        students all over the world. Realizing that students would not have
        access to traditional summer schooling and camps, Kushal and Anurag
        realized that kids would not have much to do over the summer.
      </p>

      <p>
        The two brothers decided to start Helping Hands, an organization that
        offers free math and science classes, conducted online for middle and
        high school students across the United States. We hope to serve all
        students and grow as an organization, helping people who need it the
        most.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside>
      <h2 class="quotes-heading">What people say</h2>

      <div class="quotes">
        {testimonials.map((t) => (
          <figure class="quote">
            <blockquote><p>{t.quote}</p></blockquote>
            <figcaption>
              {t.attribution}{t.role && <span class="quote-role">{t.role}</span>}
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <h2>Why we keep teaching</h2>

  <div class="split">
    <div class="split-text">
      <p>
        When we started Helping Hands, we wanted to give students a place where
        they could ask questions, make mistakes, and learn without feeling
        pressured or judged. Over time, we&rsquo;ve watched students who once
        struggled with a concept begin to understand it, gain confidence, and
        even start helping others. Those moments are what keep us going.
      </p>

      <p>
        Teaching has also taught us a lot. Every student we meet has a different
        story, a different way of learning, and something new to teach us. Seeing
        their excitement when something finally clicks, hearing them ask
        questions they were once afraid to ask, and watching their confidence
        grow reminds us why we chose to do this in the first place.
      </p>

      <p>
        We know that a few hours of teaching each week may seem small, but to us,
        every student matters. If we can make learning a little easier, help
        someone believe in themselves a little more, or simply be there when they
        need an extra hand, then our time is worth it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="split-media">
      <img src={story.teachingImage} alt={story.teachingAlt} />
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>